>
> I don't know, but I suspect that it might not currently be possible for a
> container to hold a living monster.

   You are correct. QM boxes are a special case; they use the 'spe' flag
to represent whether or not the box contains a Schroedinger's Cat, as
Janis replied elsethread. However, there is no way to store an arbitrary
monster inside a box; that would require extra infrastructure.

> Further questions: Do QM boxes weigh more than normal boxes?

   Yes, by the weight of one (1) housecat.

> If you drop one in water, does the cat "inside" drown?

   Boxes are waterproof; nothing in them is damaged by water. Therefore,
it is consistent that the cat "inside" is also unaffected by being
underwater. :)  As long as we ignore the limited air supply, that is...
but then these /are/ "large" boxes!

